\label{Niku.existence}
A nondegenerate even lattice $S$ admits a primitive extension to the
lattice $L$ if and only if the following conditions are satisfied:
\begin{enumerate}
	\item $\sigma^{+}(S)\leqslant 3$, $\sigma^{-}(S)\leqslant 19$, and
	$\operatorname{rk}S+\ell(\operatorname{discr} S)\leqslant 22$;
	\item $( -1)^{\sigma^{+}(S)-1}|\operatorname{discr} S|
	\equiv \det_{p} S \pmod{\bigl(\mathbb{Z}^{*}_{p}\bigr)^{2}}$
	for all odd prime numbers $p$ such that
	$\operatorname{rk}S+\ell_{p}(S)=22$;
	\item either $\operatorname{rk}S+\ell_{2}(S)<22$, or
	$(\operatorname{discr} S)_{2}$ is odd, or
	$|\operatorname{discr} S|
	\equiv \pm\det_{2}S \pmod{\bigl(\mathbb{Z}^{*}_{2}\bigr)^{2}}$.
